  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rights-based rainforest solutions at scale - Brazil</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rights-based sustainable management of large, contiguous rainforest areas in the Brazilian Amazon, including local sustainable management, improvement of policy and legal frameworks on forest and rights, and the engagement of commercial actors, to stop or reduce deforestation; together with civil society patners. indigenous peoples and local communities in Brazil. Partners tentatively include FOIRN, ATIX, CPI Acre, IEPE, CNS and Instituto Escolhas, in addition to ISA. Rainforest Foundation Norway prioritizes women (and youth) in all their projects. Their projects are designed so as to ensure real engagement by women (and youth) in all processes and at all levels throughout project implementation, including in the more patriarchal tribal systems (to the degree possible).</narrative>
  </description>
